And then I report back to my superiors at Bloomingdale's, so...

246
00:16:17,930 --> 00:16:20,470
And obviously, in this case...

247
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:23,390
...I am going to report back:

248
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:26,730
"U.S.A. Not ready."

249
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,570
- Maybe in L.A.     - Yes.

250
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:32,820
- There you go.     - So have you kids eaten yet?

251
00:16:32,990 --> 00:16:35,530
Well, ahem, we were going to do that after. I mean, um...

252
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,990
- Next.     - Well, we're starving.

253
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,790
Why don't we just all go get something to eat?

254
00:16:41,950 --> 00:16:47,830
Yeah, well, ha, ha, no use wasting this baby just lying around the house.

255
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:51,380
So we'll go eat.

256
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:53,260
You'll wear that.

257
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,760
We'll be eating and, of course, you'll be wearing that.

258
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:01,930
Dude, I am sorry about what I said.

259
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:05,100
Nope, nope, you're right. It is a ridiculous name.

260
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:08,600
- It's not that bad.     - Yes, it is.

261
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,320
From now on, I have no first name.

262
00:17:13,190 --> 00:17:16,450
So you're just Bing?

263
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,280
I have no name.

264
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,240
So, what are we supposed to call you?

265
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:27,000
Okay, uh, for now, temporarily, you can call me...

266
00:17:27,790 --> 00:17:29,170
...Clint.

267
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:33,550
No way are you cool enough to pull off "Clint."

268
00:17:33,710 --> 00:17:36,050
Okay, so, what name am I cool enough to pull off?

269
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:38,050
Um, Gene.

270
00:17:41,010 --> 00:17:44,220
It's Clint. It's Clint.

271
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,640
- See you later, Gene.     - Bye, Gene.

272
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,650
It's Clint. Clint!

273
00:17:53,570 --> 00:17:55,360
What's up with Gene?

274
00:17:59,410 --> 00:18:01,780
- You wore your nightie to dinner?     - Oh, yeah.

275
00:18:01,950 --> 00:18:05,830
And the best part though, was when the waiter spilled water down my back.

276
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,120
I jumped up and my boob popped out.

277
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:10,080
- Oh, my God.     - Oh, no.

278
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:12,090
Yeah, it's all right. I got nice boobs.

279
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:17,800
So I just picked up a message from Emily.

280
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:21,390
She and Susan are going to a poetry reading together.

281
00:18:21,550 --> 00:18:23,760
- So?     - So?

282
00:18:23,930 --> 00:18:25,720
Poetry?

283
00:18:25,890 --> 00:18:28,100
Susan's gay.

284
00:18:28,270 --> 00:18:30,600
They're being gay together.

285
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:35,110
- Emily's straight.     - Oh, wake up.

286
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:40,280
Carol really messed you up.

287
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:41,860
Excuse me?

288
00:18:42,030 --> 00:18:48,290
She turned you into this untrusting, crazy, jealous sycophant.

289
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:54,750
All right, so I don't know what "sycophant" means, but the rest is right.

290
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:59,420
I don't know what you're talking about. I am not a crazy, jealous person.

291
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:04,470
- What?     - She's totally right.

292
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:07,350
When we were together, you got all freaked out about Mark...

293
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:10,060
...and there was nothing going on.     - This makes sense.

294
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:11,730
It does not.

295
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:14,730
Sure it does. In high school, you weren't jealous at all...

296
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:17,690
...even though all your girlfriends were cheating on you.

297
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:22,740
All right, so up until '92, '93, he was very trusting.

298
00:19:22,910 --> 00:19:26,530
Then '94 hit, Carol left him, and bam. Paranoid City.

299
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:27,990
Yeah.

300
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,500
Absolutely, absolutely.

301
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:30,830
This is so much fun.

302
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,880
This is not fun.

303
00:19:35,170 --> 00:19:37,840
Look, all we're trying to say is...

304
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:41,630
...don't let what happened with Carol ruin what you've got with Emily.

305
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:45,850
The '92 Ross wouldn't.

306
00:19:51,230 --> 00:19:54,350
I still think I was right about that whole Mark thing, though.

307
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:58,150
Wha...? Well, you know what? I hope Emily is a lesbian.

308
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:06,990
Drum roll.

309
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:08,870
Okay. Okay.

310
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,580
All right.

311
00:20:11,250 --> 00:20:15,460
Help. Am I a Mark or a John?

312
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:19,300
Ehh, you're not tall enough to be a Mark.

313
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:22,260
But you might make a good Barney.

314
00:20:24,010 --> 00:20:25,260
All right, look, I am serious.

315
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:27,890
Tomorrow at 3:30, I'm going to the courthouse.

316
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,720
You're actually going through with this?

317
00:20:29,890 --> 00:20:32,640
Hey, look, this name has been holding me back my entire life.

318
00:20:32,810 --> 00:20:36,650
Okay, it's probably why kids picked on me and why I never do well with women.

319
00:20:36,810 --> 00:20:40,570
So as of 4:00 tomorrow, I'm either gonna be Mark Johnson or John Markson.

320
00:20:42,150 --> 00:20:45,200
You've got problems because of you, not your name.

321
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:51,040
This has got to stop. Chandler is a great name.

322
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,870
In fact...

323
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,460
Yes.

324
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:58,830
I'm sorry, I know you really wanted me to name the baby Joey.

325
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:03,260
But... So I'm gonna name the baby Chandler.

326
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:07,260
Really?

327
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:09,470
Yeah, but you have to keep the name too.

328
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:12,010
- Okay, thanks.     - Okay.

329
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:14,140
- You want to hug it out?     - Yeah.

330
00:21:17,730 --> 00:21:19,810
Okay, I'm gonna go tell Frank and Alice right now.

331
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:24,490
- Bye, Pheebs.     - Okay, bye.

332
00:21:37,870 --> 00:21:42,000
Flight 004 is now arriving at Gate 17.

333
00:21:45,840 --> 00:21:48,130
- Nice luggage.     - I was going to say.

334
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:55,640
- I missed you.     - Oh, I missed you too.

335
00:21:55,810 --> 00:21:57,520
Thanks for everything, I had a great time.

336
00:21:57,690 --> 00:21:59,650
Oh, so did I.

337
00:22:01,270 --> 00:22:03,070
No tongue.

